Well, that's the thing, could we?

Definitions were sometimes written sloppily without giving much
thought as to how they would be used, sometimes interpreted
sloppily without taking what the definition says at face value, and
sometimes a bit of both. A rule and a property are somewhat different
things. If a "rule" is what goes in x3, {lo ka ...} is not quite the
 right
thing to use there. If {lo ka ...} is what goes in x3, then describing
 it
as a "rule" is not quite right. In that case the definition should have
been something more like:

 x1 is (n)th among x2 ordered by how much property x3 they have.

